<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb imported vehicle sales up 8.6% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb imported vehicle sales up 8.6% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of imported vehicles in Japan rose 8.6 percent in February from a year earlier to 36,759 units, the Japan Automobile Importers' Association (JAIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the second successive month that sales had risen on a year-on-year basis and was also a record high for that month, surpassing the previous February record of 33,839 marked last year.  </p>
<p> Cars total		33,750  up   5.5 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc   21,237  down 7.5 percent</p>
<p>- Cars under 2000 cc  12,513  up  38.6 percent</p>
<p> Trucks total	     3,009  up  63.3 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy		    1,731  down 1.8 percent</p>
<p> - Light		    1,278	     nil</p>
<p> Buses			  nil  vs	 3</p>
<p>Exporting countries and selected makers' car sales in Japan in February, with percentage changes from a year earlier:  German total		   17,813  up   25.8 percent</p>
<p>  Volkswagen Audi Group	6,324  up   42.6 percent</p>
<p>  -Volkswagen	 5,116  up   38.8 percent</p>
<p>  -Audi		 1,208  up   61.1 percent</p>
<p>  Adam Opel			3,690  up   14.3 percent</p>
<p>  BMW		   3,202  up   47.8 percent</p>
<p>  Mercedes-Benz     3,701  up    7.6 percent</p>
<p>  Ford-Werke AG	 715  down  2.3 percent</p>
<p>  Porsche		 162  up   11.0 percent</p>
<p> United States total	   7,547  down 33.9 percent</p>
<p>  Honda USA	   2,939  down 38.7 percent</p>
<p>  Ford Motor	     1,089  up    8.5 percent</p>
<p>  General Motors	1,364  down 31.5 percent</p>
<p>  Toyota		  581  down 77.7 percent</p>
<p>  Chrysler		 1,291  up   40.5 percent</p>
<p> Sweden total		    1,856  up    2.9 percent</p>
<p>  Volvo			    1,814  up    6.7 percent</p>
<p>  Saab				  42  down 59.6 percent</p>
<p> Britain total		   3,503  up   79.7 percent</p>
<p>  Rover group		    3,136  up   90.4 percent</p>
<p>  Jaguar			    241   up   18.1 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     67   up  191.3 percent</p>
<p> France total			956  up   35.8 percent</p>
<p>  Peugeot Citroen		  771  up   56.7 percent</p>
<p>  - Peugeot			  394  up   77.5 percent</p>
<p>  - Citroen			  377  up   39.6 percent</p>
<p>  Renault			    185  down 12.7 percent</p>
